                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "19378371",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198044307306",
                            "num_reviews": 28,
                            "playtime_forever": 34,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 34,
                            "last_played": 1448843639
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game looks and feels like a mobile port: There is no in-game options menu besides simply turning music and sound on or off. The UI is dominated by massively oversized buttons. There are no tooltips, nor use of the right mouse button, nor clicking and dragging. In addition, the game feels cheap; several spelling errors were noted while playing, and the graphics are simple and repetitive. The turn-based gameplay itself is a bit simple and dull. It plays almost like a board game; save for the twist that the board rotates under you with each turn.\n\nIf it was on my phone, I might keep it around to play through the campaign whenever I was in an area without mobile data. Long story short, you get what you pay for, and this feels like a $0.49 game; but even then, there are many free games on Steam or elsewhere that I would recommend over this.\n\nDISCLAIMER: I was given a free key for this game, and offered additional compensation to play it and write a review. Despite that, I have tried to give my opinion as honestly as possible.",
